# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The AI assistant's model.
#
# ALL OPTIONAL. Without any of this the screener, filters, sorting, columns and
# charts all work; only the chat assistant is disabled, and it says so rather
# than failing obscurely.
#
# Any provider that speaks the OpenAI wire format works — which is all of the
# ones below. Switching is these three variables, not a code change.
#
# What the assistant needs to work well:
#   - TOOL CALLING. Without it the model can talk but cannot drive the app.
#   - Room in the rate limit. One multi-step turn here costs roughly 7,000
#     tokens, because every step re-sends the system prompt and tool schemas.
#     A cap of 8,000 tokens a minute therefore fits about one turn a minute.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

LLM_API_KEY=
# LLM_BASE_URL=
# LLM_MODEL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where to point it. Free tiers change constantly — check the current quota
# before assuming any of these is roomier than what you have.
#
# Nothing hosted is truly unlimited. Free tiers are rate-limited, credit-
# limited, or both. The only uncapped option is the last one.
#
# Groq — the default. Fast, but the free tier is the tightest here.
#   LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
#   LLM_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b
#   Key: https://console.groq.com/keys
#
# Google Gemini — measured as the best of these: four consecutive turns with no
# rate limit, sub-second each, against Groq's 2-15s.
#   LLM_BASE_URL=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai/
#   LLM_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash-lite
#   Key: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
#
#   PIN A VERSION. The "-latest" aliases point at the newest model, which has
#   the TIGHTEST free quota: gemini-flash-latest resolved to a model allowing
#   20 requests per day — about six questions before it stops. The quota is per
#   model, so pinning an older flash-lite gets a usable allowance. The 2.x
#   models 404 on this endpoint; 3.1-flash-lite and 3.5-flash-lite both work.
#
# Cerebras — free tier, very fast inference.
#   LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.cerebras.ai/v1
#   LLM_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b
#   Key: https://cloud.cerebras.ai
#
# OpenRouter — one key across many providers, including some free models
# (their ids end in ":free"). Useful for trying several without new accounts.
#   LLM_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
#   LLM_MODEL=<pick one that supports tools>
#   Key: https://openrouter.ai/keys
#
# Mistral — free experimental tier on their own platform.
#   LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.mistral.ai/v1
#   LLM_MODEL=mistral-small-latest
#   Key: https://console.mistral.ai
#
# DeepSeek — OpenAI-compatible and cheap, though check whether the free credits
# still apply before assuming it costs nothing.
#   LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.deepseek.com
#   LLM_MODEL=deepseek-chat
#   Key: https://platform.deepseek.com
#
# Not usable here, however they are advertised:
#   - Chat WEBSITES with no signup. They are a browser UI, not an API, so
#     nothing can call a tool through them.
#   - "gpt4free"-style proxies (g4f and friends). They reach providers' own web
#     endpoints without authorization, which breaks their terms, breaks
#     whenever the provider changes anything, and routes your prompts through
#     a third party. Not worth wiring an app to.
#
# A model on your own machine — the only genuinely unlimited and free option.
# No key, no quota, no per-token cost; you pay in hardware and speed instead.
# Ollama serves an OpenAI-compatible endpoint on port 11434:
#
#   ollama pull gpt-oss:20b        # or another tool-calling model
#   ollama serve
#   LLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
#   LLM_MODEL=gpt-oss:20b
#
# LM Studio does the same on port 1234. Leave LLM_API_KEY empty for either —
# a localhost endpoint is recognised as needing no key.
#
# The catch: a smaller local model is worse at tool calling than a hosted
# frontier one, so expect it to miss calls this app's prompt assumes. Try the
# largest one your machine will hold.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Still read if set, so an existing setup keeps working.
# GROQ_API_KEY=
